      "author": "Hollowmere team",
      "story": "Ed Calder sold nails, feed and free advice at the crossing for thirty years. When the town emptied he stayed. He hauled his best tools and the last of the nails up into the feed loft, strung cans across the office doorway, nailed the back-room doors shut and piled feed sacks behind them, then climbed into the loft and pulled the loading-bay ladder up after him. He lasted four days on what he had carried up. Thirst brought him back down, and the ladder is still standing where he left it. So is Ed, at the foot of it.",
